From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:42:06 -0400
Subject: D3D11: Sync image from storage before CPU CopyTexSubImage

Check getBaseLevel() in canCreateRenderTargetForImage and sync clean
staging images from mTexStorage via getImageAndSyncFromStorageIfNeeded
before copyFromFramebuffer so partial copies preserve existing storage
contents.

Test:
    angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*CopyTexImageTestES3.*Preserves**"
Bug: b/563355257
Change-Id: I3ad952bbd73af45e6938e43c9e1e31ce8d67437b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8452764
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Yuxin Hu <yuxinhu@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): getImageAndSyncFromStorageIfNeeded is
taken verbatim from upstream (this ANGLE revision still had the 2017-era
body that set mDirtyImages and called markClean() unconditionally, which
would discard uncommitted staging data under the new !isDirty() condition).
This revision also still routes CopyTexImage/CopyTexSubImage through the CPU
path when the D3D11 zeroMaxLodWorkaround is enabled, even for complete
levels; upstream's copyImageFromFramebufferToStaging asserts the level is
incomplete, so on that workaround path the helper first syncs the staging
image from mTexStorage via getImageAndSyncFromStorageIfNeeded and keeps the
pre-existing onStateChange(DirtyBitsFlagged) signal. Reviewer attention
requested on that branch-only path.

